// Canonical source: a path into a primitive value. c.v is an int, and an int
// has no fields, so c.v.w = 4; answers field/not-found instead of writing
// into an int.
// Answer: "BML-HATI-UNSUPPORTED field/not-found".
class C : Object { section [public] { int v; } }
C c = new C();
c.v.w = 4;
return c.v;
